Judging by how quickly my mail to you was spit back at me I'm not
surprised...

I think you're on the right track by thinking something weird in your
config.sys or autoexec.bat files could be messing up with the shell 
escape.  Instead of having people send theirs to you to compare, why not
try this?:

Make a disk bootable with format a: /s.  Make a config.sys on that disk
with just a "device=c:\ansi.sys" (or wherever it is).  Boot from that
disk, run NetHack, do a shell escape.  If that works, it shouldn't take
too long to find the offending TSR or whatever.  If it doesn't, time to
look elsewhere...


